===Etymology===
As a noun, from {{inh|en|enm|chep}}, from {{inh|en|ang|cēap|t=trade, market, value}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*kaup}}. As a verb, from {{inh|en|enm|chepen}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ċēapian|t=to buy, bargain, trade}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*kaupōn}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*kaupōną}}, a verbal derivative of {{m|gem-pro|*kaupô|t=trader}}, from {{der|en|la|caupō}}.

The adjective originated as a shortening of Middle and Early Modern English {{m|enm|good}} {{m|enm|cheap}}, literally “good purchase” (as in “that was good cheap”, i.e. “that was [a] good purchase”). Compare {{m+|nl|goedkoop}}, {{m+|fr|bon marché}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|entry=cheap|pos=adj|id=9698883610|date=June 2025}}</ref>

{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|sco|chepe|t=to sell}}, {{m|sco|chape|t=sale price}}, {{cog|frr|keap|t=purchase}}, {{cog|fy|keap|t=purchase, buy, acquisition}}, {{cog|nl|koop|t=buy, purchase, deal}}, {{m|nl|kopen|t=to buy, purchase, shop}}, {{cog|nds|kopen|t=to buy}}, {{cog|de|Kauf|t=trade, traffic, bargain, purchase, buy}}, {{m|de|kaufen|t=to buy}}, {{cog|sv|köp|t=bargain, purchase}}, {{m|sv|köpa|t=to buy, purchase}}, {{cog|nn|kjøpa|t=to buy, purchase}}, {{cog|is|kaup|t=purchase, bargain}}, {{m|is|kaupa|t=to purchase}}; also borrowed as {{cog|fi|kauppa|t=shop, trade}}, {{cog|ru|купить|t=to purchase}}, {{cog|cu|коупити|t=to purchase}}, {{cog|bg|ку́пя|t=to purchase}}, {{cog|sh|купити|t=to purchase}}, {{cog|cs|koupit|t=to purchase}}, {{cog|pl|kupić|t=to purchase}}.
